[123.475778, "i", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 release summary\n\n## What was wrong\n\n- Calendar arithmetic clamped every anchor to the 28th and advanced from the\n  previous renewal, losing month-end and leap-day anchors.\n- Proration used fixed 30/365-day periods and credited the old plan at the\n  change-date price rather than the price originally billed.\n- Monthly/annual switches were prorated instead of starting a full new cycle.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Renewals clamp to the target month's actual last day and always derive from\n  the original anchor. Cycle lookup is constant-time for bulk repricing.\n- Credits and same-interval charges use actual cycle days; credits use the\n  cycle-start price and new charges use the change-date price.\n- Interval switches charge the full new price and re-anchor on the change date.\n- Half-even rounding uses exact integer arithmetic, independent of Decimal\n  precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python -m unittest discover -s tests`: 25 tests pass, incl"]
[123.476039, "i", "uding the existing\n  bulk performance check and seven additional regression tests.\n- All 10 finance examples verified through `python -m billing preview`, including\n  line amounts, service periods, totals, amount due, and carried credit.\n- No existing tests, finance fixtures, performance budgets, or known-failure\n  settings were changed.\nEOF\ncd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests\n"]
[123.476179, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[123.476201, "o", "uding the existing\r\n  bulk performance check and seven additional regression tests.\r\n- All 10 finance examples verified through `python -m billing preview`, including\r\n  line amounts, service periods, totals, amount due, and carried credit.\r\n- No existing tests, finance fixtures, performance budgets, or known-failure\r\n  settings were changed.\r\nEOF\r\ncd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests\r\n\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.477885, "o", "# BILL-212 release summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## What was wrong\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Calendar arithmetic clamped every anchor to the 28th and advanced from the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   previous renewal, losing month-end and leap-day anchors.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Proration used fixed 30/365-day periods and credited the old plan at the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   change-date price rather than the price originally billed.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Monthly/annual switches were prorated instead of starting a full new cycle.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## What changed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Renewals clamp to the target month's actual last day and always derive from\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   the original anchor. Cycle lookup is constant-time for bulk repricing.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Credits and same-interval charges use actual cycle days; credits use the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   cycle-start price and new charges use the change-date price.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.478008, "o", "- Interval switches charge the full new price and re-anchor on the change date.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Half-even rounding uses exact integer arithmetic, independent of Decimal\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   precision. Public function signatures are unchanged.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Verification\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - `python -m unittest discover -s tests`: 25 tests pass, including the existing\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   bulk performance check and seven additional regression tests.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - All 10 finance examples verified through `python -m billing preview`, including\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   line amounts, service periods, totals, amount due, and carried credit.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - No existing tests, finance fixtures, performance budgets, or known-failure\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   settings were changed.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[123.4792, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@2c7807260503:/app# "]
[123.479237, "o", "cd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
